    {
      "day": "Wednesday",
      "name": "Quick Grilled Cheese and Tomato Soup",
      "source_url": "https://diethood.com/classic-tomato-soup-and-grilled-cheese/",
      "source_name": "Diethood",
      "servings": "4",
      "prep_time": "10 min",
      "cook_time": "20 min",
      "nonna_says": "Start the soup first, garlic in good oil, then your tomatoes, broth, a splash of cream, and let it simmer while you build the sandwiches. Now listen, on the bread you use mayonnaise, not butter. A thin even swipe, corner to corner, on the outside of every slice. The oil in the mayo crisps the bread harder than butter ever did and gives you that tangy, almost-savory crust I always loved. Pile good cheese in the middle, not so much it slides around like a bad decision. Low and steady on the griddle until each side is deep, deep gold and the inside is melted through. Blend the soup smooth, taste for salt, pinch of sugar if the tomatoes are sharp. Cut the sandwiches into dunkers and feed your people.",
